 java variable - A variable is a named memory location used to store data.

Every variable in Java must have:
			Once declared, a variable cannot change its data type.
			A data type
			A unique name
			A value (optional at declaration)
			
Naming Rules for Variables - Follow these rules:
		
		Can contain letters, digits, _, $
		Cannot start with a digit
		Cannot use Java keywords
		Case-sensitive
		 
java literals - A literal is the actual fixed value assigned to a variable.
 
 Example: java
		int activeUsers = 5000;
		Here:
		
		activeUsers → variable
		5000 → literal
		Java supports multiple types of literals.